                <pb facs="0369" n="269" sameAs="frus:frus1934v01/pg269"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A5/106: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1934-06-22T19:00:00+01:00">June 22, 1934—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 22—2:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>349. From Davis. Embassy’s telegram 344, June 22, noon. Bingham and I feel that
                    the program proposed by the British at the meeting of experts yesterday is so
                    unacceptable from our point of view that we should tell the British we think it
                    inadvisable to enter upon technical discussions on such a basis. We will,
                    however, cable later our more considered views as to the course we should
                    pursue. [Davis.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bingham</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
